# The container build (docker/Dockerfile) uses the repository root as its
# context, and this is an ALLOWLIST: everything is excluded, then the three
# files the Dockerfile COPYs are let back in. So a build can never sweep up
# .git, target/, a local .env holding API keys, or anything else in a working
# checkout — and the context the engine uploads is a few kilobytes.
#
# Docker and Podman both read this file from the context root.
**
!install.sh
